# Huawei VRP `display device elabel brief` parser (Phase 49-D-12).
#
# Sample input (templates/samples/huawei_CX-WH-RUITONG-26F-SWL3-HW-S8700_display_device_elabel_brief.txt):
#   Equipment SN(ESN): 102599861598
#   License ESN: 102599861598
#   ----- (header rule) -----
#   SlotID     Sub    Type                     SN                       P/N
#   ----- (header rule) -----
#   --         --     BackPlane                102599861598             02116318
#   1          --     LSG7G48VX1E0             102599806091             03050DLX
#   5          --     LSG7SRUEX1C0             102599806032             03050CTT-001
#   FAN1       --     FAN-240SM-B              5B2599001775             02122824
#   PWR1       --     PAC3KS54-DF              2102312TCAJVR8000929     02312TCA
#
# Field semantics:
#   SLOTID  — physical identifier: "--" (BackPlane) | numeric slot (1..N) | "FANn" | "PWRn"
#   TYPE    — module model string (BackPlane / LSG7G48VX1E0 / LSG7SRUEX1C0 / FAN-240SM-B / PAC3KS54-DF)
#   SN      — vendor-issued serial number for this physical entity
#   PN      — vendor part number (P/N column)
#
# Strategy: emit ONE record per data row. The chassis ESN (from
# "Equipment SN(ESN):" line) is parsed separately by enrichChassisSerial
# via a regex — keeping textfsm focused on the tabular data.
#
# The project's homegrown textfsm parser (internal/templates/textfsm.go)
# applies strings.TrimSpace to each line BEFORE rule matching, so
# rule patterns should NOT use leading \s+. The Sub column is
# always "--" on the S8700 but the pattern tolerates any non-space
# token (e.g. "1" for stacked sub-slots) to support future models.
#
# Component type mapping (handled in collector, not template):
#   - SLOTID == "--"          → skip (BackPlane = chassis, handled by ParseDisplayDeviceEsn)
#   - SLOTID starts "FAN"     → ComponentTypeFan
#   - SLOTID starts "PWR"     → ComponentTypePower
#   - numeric + TYPE contains "SRU"/"MPU"/"SFU" → ComponentTypeEngine
#   - numeric + other TYPE    → ComponentTypeCard

Value SLOTID (\S+)
Value TYPE (\S+)
Value SN (\S+)
Value PN (\S+)

Start
  ^${SLOTID}\s+\S+\s+${TYPE}\s+${SN}\s+${PN}\s*$$ -> Record
